From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 16:42:16 -0300
Subject: Provide fmt/spdlog for system oxen-logging headers

The system liboxen-logging headers include <fmt/...>/<spdlog/...> but its
pkg-config exposes neither; attach the bundled (header-only) fmt/spdlog to the
imported oxen::logging target so consumers can compile its headers on distros
whose system fmt/spdlog are too old.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 external/CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/external/CMakeLists.txt b/external/CMakeLists.txt
index 932e2e1..ad0338f 100644
--- a/external/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/external/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -58,6 +58,11 @@ if(NOT TARGET oxen::logging)
     if(BUILD_STATIC_DEPS OR DEPS_FORCE_SUBMODULE OR DEPS_FORCE_liboxen-logging_SUBMODULE)
         set(OXEN_LOGGING_FORCE_SUBMODULES ON)
     endif()
+    # This distro's system fmt/spdlog are too old, so load.cmake falls back to the bundled
+    # submodules.  Those must be header-only: with BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON they would otherwise be
+    # built as shared libraries that get linked into libsession-util but never installed.
+    set(OXEN_LOGGING_FMT_HEADER_ONLY ON)
+    set(OXEN_LOGGING_SPDLOG_HEADER_ONLY ON)
     include(session-router/external/oxen-libquic/external/oxen-logging/cmake/load.cmake)
 endif()
 
